+## Voyage: Spec the event-binding helper capture-flag defect
 
 ### Situation
 
-External browser acceptance suite (Cypress) reports 5 failures:
-1. Mark all as completed — `cy.eq()` detached from DOM
-2. Clear complete state — `cy.eq()` detached from DOM
-3. Mark items as complete — `cy.find()` detached from DOM
-4. Unmark items as complete — `cy.find()` detached from DOM
-5. Save edits on blur — expected `<li.editing>` to contain new text
+External browser acceptance suite (Cypress) reports 1 remaining failure:
+- Save edits on blur — expected `<li.editing>` to contain "buy some sausages"
 
-All 5 stem from the same root cause: the `render()` function in `js/app.js` unconditionally removes ALL existing `<li>` children and deletes every entry from the `existingItems` tracking map, then recreates every node from scratch. Any browser-held reference (from `cy.eq()`, `cy.find()`, or a blur event target) is invalidated.
+The prior 4 Cypress failures (detached DOM from `cy.eq()` / `cy.find()`) were resolved by commits `c0eee4c` and `1fb3dfe`, which replaced the innerHTML rebuild with in-place node mutation.
 
-### What was done
+The remaining failure has a different root cause: the `on()` helper function at `js/app.js:72` silently drops the `useCapture` argument:
+
+```javascript
+function on(el, evt, fn) {
+    el.addEventListener(evt, fn);  // ignores 4th argument
+}
+```
 
-Promoted 5 `@captain @conformance` scenarios to binding `@conformance` status:
+The blur handler is registered as `on(todoList, 'blur', handler, true)`, but `true` is never forwarded to `addEventListener`. In a real browser, `blur` does not bubble, so the delegated handler on `todoList` never fires. The harness passes because it dispatches `new Event('blur', {bubbles: true})` which forces bubbling.
+
